  message: "SATISFIED in PR #743, with behavioural evidence on the item's own repro re-run through the production derivation + matcher (`_derive_auto_imports_from_io_primitives` -> `_build_callee_index` -> `_match_propagation_entry`, shipped go catalogue):\n  go:bufio:0-0:NewScanner:unresolved  unstamped     SOURCE untrusted_input/ipc_recv   (was None)\n  go:bufio:0-0:NewScanner:unresolved  host_path     SOURCE None                       (unchanged)\n  go:bufio:0-0:NewScanner:unresolved  std_stream    SOURCE untrusted_input/ipc_recv   (unchanged)\n  go:bufio:0-0:ReadString:unresolved  unstamped     SOURCE None  (fallback fs_read mints nothing -- WI-vutav's asymmetry kept)\n  go:io:0-0:WriteString:unresolved    unstamped     SINK host_fs      (unchanged, and would have been None under a verbatim mirror)\n  c:unistd:0-0:write:unresolved       unstamped     SINK host_fs      (unchanged)\n  haskell:System.IO:0-0:hPutStr       unstamped     SINK host_fs      (unchanged)\nAll pinned in packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_target_kind_fallback_entries.py.\n\nMECHANISM. `io_boundary.target_kind_fallback_boundaries(catalog)` reads, per gated primitive, the FIRST row of the same reordered list `classify_call` selects from (abstains_to row after `_apply_abstention_targets`, else registry order); the derivation marks that row's entry `abstention_fallback=True` on TaintSource and TaintSink; `_target_kind_admits` admits an unconditional entry, a gated entry whose boundary the stamp resolves to in the entry's own direction, or on abstention the fallback entry alone. One fact, one home: neither consumer re-derives \"first\".\n\nCORPUS EFFECT (six repos, read side; vutav_reads_09032026/bc_compare_readside.out): 14 bufio rows gained a stamp (2 net_stream -> net_recv, 12 in_memory incl. 7 reads); 12 constructors stay unstamped and now MINT ipc_recv, each read back: 3 TRUE (alertmanager cluster/tls_connection.go:136 TLS conn via a struct field; caddy fastcgi client.go:219 `r := c.Do(p, req)`; cilium connectivity/tests/pod.go:427 `output := ...ExecInPod(...)`), 8 io.Reader / *os.File / io.ReadSeeker PARAMETERS whose callers read files (beads markdown.go:252, caddy lexer.go:79 + main.go:388, cilium ipsec_linux.go:1073, kernel_hz.go:84, mountinfo.go:40, feature-helm-generator/main.go:218, hubble io_reader_observer.go:39) -- INV-bagok's ruling accepted this trade for the boundary tagger; the taint side now carries it too, and the lever is caller-side parameter typing, not this item -- and 1 behind a multi-line signature (cilium klog_bridge.go:137).\n\nLIVE RE-RUN (fallback_repro.py, tree named in its first line; suhug_writes_09032026/after_fallback.txt):\nTREE: dev@be4c6cfd8e\n--- read side (INV-minol)\ngo       go:bufio:0-0:NewScanner:unresolved            kinds=()               SOURCE=('untrusted_input', 'ipc_recv')  SINK=None\ngo       go:bufio:0-0:NewReader:unresolved             kinds=()               SOURCE=('untrusted_input', 'ipc_recv')  SINK=None\ngo       go:bufio:0-0:NewScanner:unresolved            kinds=('host_path',)   SOURCE=None  SINK=None\ngo       go:bufio:0-0:NewScanner:unresolved            kinds=('std_stream',)  SOURCE=('untrusted_input', 'ipc_recv')  SINK=None\ngo       go:bufio:0-0:NewScanner:unresolved            kinds=('net_stream',)  SOURCE=('untrusted_input', 'net_recv')  SINK=None\ngo       go:bufio:0-0:ReadString:unresolved            kinds=()               SOURCE=None  SINK=None\n--- write side (WI-suhug)\ngo       go:io:0-0:WriteString:unresolved              kinds=()               SOURCE=None  SINK=host_fs\ngo       go:io:0-0:WriteString:unresolved              kinds=('pipe',)        SOURCE=None  SINK=ipc\ngo       go:fmt:0-0:Fprintf:unresolved                 kinds=()               SOURCE=None  SINK=logging\ngo       go:fmt:0-0:Fprintf:unresolved                 kinds=('net_stream',)  SOURCE=None  SINK=network\ngo       go:fmt:0-0:Fprintf:unresolved                 kinds=('host_path',)   SOURCE=None  SINK=host_fs\n--- unchanged elsewhere\nc        c:unistd:0-0:write:unresolved                 kinds=()               SOURCE=None  SINK=host_fs\nhaskell  haskell:System.IO:0-0:hPutStr:unresolved      kinds=()               SOURCE=None  SINK=host_fs"  # 93db
